# Vercel serves the static frontend in web/ and nothing else.
#
# Everything Python is excluded on purpose. Vercel decides a project is Python
# by finding an api/ directory and a requirements.txt, so leaving those in the
# upload makes it install a Builder and try to run a serverless function. That
# is what produced the "@vercel/python (pin-version-mismatch)" build failure.
# With them ignored there is no build step at all — just files being served —
# so the deploy needs no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, no database, and no secrets.
#
# The backend still lives in this repo and still runs locally and on Render.
# To put it back on Vercel, drop these Python entries and restore the
# functions/rewrites block in vercel.json.

api/
app/
scripts/
tests/
migrations/
config/
requirements.txt
requirements-server.txt
*.py
setup.sh
render.yaml

# Local artefacts
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Secrets — a static deploy needs none of these.
.env
*.env
service-account*.json
credentials*.json

*.md
.git/
.claude/
